1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:07,100
["You're My Favorite Song"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

2
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:10,467
<i>Previously on You're My Favorite
Song...</i>

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,233
<i>I won't allow your resort
to succeed.</i>

4
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:15,800
<i> I'll give you even more,</i>

5
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:17,967
<i>as long as you make sure
you do a good job.</i>

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,967
<i> Leave it to us, Miss Serina.</i>

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,400
<i>Their grand opening
won't push through.</i>

8
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:25,433
<i>You know, he's one of the people
who vandalized our resort.</i>

9
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:27,767
<i>Kaila, do you know
where I can find them?</i>

10
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,733
<i>They hang out at the milk tea
shop.</i>

11
00:00:29,867 --> 00:00:31,600
<i> Boba Ka Tea.</i>

12
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,933
<i> There's nothing I can do now.</i>

13
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:34,100
<i> It already happened.</i>

14
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,167
<i> We lost.</i>

15
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,700
<i> Do you think I wanted this?</i>

16
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:39,367
<i> I hate losing too, Angel.</i>

17
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,767
<i>Winning that QuizCon
meant so much to me.</i>

18
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,100
<i>If you're fighting for yourself
and your image,</i>

19
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:47,233
<i>I'm fighting for my grandfather.</i>

20
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,533
<i> You're really cruel.</i>

21
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:52,433
<i>All you ever think
about is yourself.</i>

22
00:00:55,633 --> 00:00:57,233
<i>These are tickets
to Siklab's concert</i>

23
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:58,967
<i>here in Solmera City next month.</i>

24
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,767
<i>-These are hard to get, right?
-Exactly.</i>

25
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,633
<i>So we can definitely sell these</i>

26
00:01:03,767 --> 00:01:06,100
<i>for more than 15,000 pesos,
right?</i>

27
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,467
<i>Someone sent money
to my e-wallet.</i>

28
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,867
<i>What was that 15,000 peso
withdrawal</i>

29
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,200
<i> from your bank account for?</i>

30
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:15,733
<i> Are you for real, Calix?</i>

31
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,767
<i>Why are you buying
Angel's ticket?</i>

32
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,667
<i>If she loses her grandfather,
she'll lose her drive to study.</i>

33
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,633
<i>Don't tell me you're falling
for that freak.</i>

34
00:01:22,767 --> 00:01:24,967
<i> You swear to me,</i>

35
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:26,300
<i>no one can ever know about this.</i>

36
00:01:28,233 --> 00:01:31,133
<i>Randel, Miguel looks exhausted.</i>

37
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:33,067
<i> The kid is completely drained.</i>

38
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:36,033
<i>They've been doing nonstop
local tours with Siklab.</i>

39
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:38,900
<i>We still have international tour
dates to announce.</i>

40
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:40,833
<i> As Miguel's manager,</i>

41
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,133
<i> your job is to make sure he
looks good in front of his fans!</i>

42
00:01:45,267 --> 00:01:47,967
<i>Not to give me
unsolicited advice.</i>

43
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:49,367
<i> Are you okay?</i>

44
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:50,200
<i> Are you okay?</i>

45
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:52,100
<i> The patient is stable now.</i>

46
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:54,267
<i> He can go home after two days.</i>

47
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,233
<i>- Thank you.
- Thank you, Doc.</i>

48
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:57,167
<i>- Thank you.
- You're welcome.</i>

49
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,600
<i>- Thank you.
- Excuse me.</i>

50
00:01:58,733 --> 00:01:59,667
Yes.

51
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,467
[BEBE SIGHS]

52
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:09,667
<i>♪ 'Cause baby
you are my favorite song ♪</i>

53
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:13,067
<i>♪ I'll put you on repeat
all night ♪</i>

54
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:17,067
<i>♪ I know that
I'll never move on ♪</i>

55
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:20,733
<i>♪ My first right
where I belong ♪</i>

56
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:27,367
<i>♪ You are my first heartbeat
song ♪</i>

57
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,700
[BRIGHT MUSIC]

58
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:43,433
[XAVI GRUNTS]

59
00:02:43,567 --> 00:02:46,733
[DRILL WHIRRING]

60
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:54,333
[XAVI EXHALES]

61
00:02:55,067 --> 00:02:57,900
Grandpa Xavi, are you sure
you're up for this already?

62
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,100
Me? This is easy for me.

63
00:03:04,167 --> 00:03:05,567
Zion.

64
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:06,767
- What?
- Yes?

65
00:03:07,067 --> 00:03:09,133
Does this grandfather
look like he has cancer?

66
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,233
Oh, Grandpa Xavi, not at all.

67
00:03:12,367 --> 00:03:13,700
You actually look even younger.

68
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:16,000
- It's like we're the same age.
- That's what I thought.

69
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:18,333
Look. I'm carrying all of these
with no trouble at all.

70
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:21,433
Beautiful.

71
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:28,933
[SOFT MUSIC]

72
00:03:31,067 --> 00:03:34,267
Beverly, my child,
what's wrong now?

73
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,333
You can see everyone's
having a good time here,

74
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,200
then you walk in.

75
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:40,767
You look so down.

76
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,033
What's the problem?

77
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,700
I know who was behind the
destruction of our resort.

78
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,533
Mama Bebe, who was it?

79
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:56,400
My dear sister, Serina.

80
00:03:57,133 --> 00:04:02,233
[TENSE MUSIC]

81
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:09,567
-Fix that.
-Hey, Mau, come visit our booth.

82
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,133
- Hold on. Relax.
- There.

83
00:04:11,267 --> 00:04:12,867
There you go.

84
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,367
You're visiting
from so far away.

85
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,100
You're being dramatic.

86
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:17,167
Which one?

87
00:04:18,767 --> 00:04:20,067
- Oh, double fight, huh.
- Double fight.

88
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,433
Oh no, they got it.

89
00:04:24,133 --> 00:04:26,367
Why did you destroy our resort?

90
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,967
Did someone order you to do it,

91
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:29,533
or are you just a bunch
of good-for-nothing pests

92
00:04:29,667 --> 00:04:31,167
with nothing better to do?

93
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:32,333
She's the owner of the resort.

94
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:39,333
Hey! Your character's skin
looks awesome.

95
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:40,667
-Maybe I'll delete it.
-Hey, don't!

96
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,433
Hey! If you don't tell me
who sent you,

97
00:04:43,567 --> 00:04:44,600
I'll delete this!

98
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:45,967
Don't!

99
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:46,933
What?

100
00:04:47,067 --> 00:04:48,800
Who? Who sent you?

101
00:04:48,933 --> 00:04:49,867
- Hey!
- Give me that.

102
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:50,833
I'm still in the middle
of a game.

103
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:52,400
Give it here. I'll delete
everything.

104
00:04:52,533 --> 00:04:53,767
Oh, you don't want to tell me?

105
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,667
Fine. Fine, I'm really going to
delete this.

106
00:04:57,667 --> 00:04:59,367
Well? Are you going to talk?

107
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:01,867
Who?

108
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:05,133
- It was...
- Who?

109
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:07,633
Miss Serina told us to do it.

110
00:05:07,767 --> 00:05:12,067
[GRIPPING MUSIC]

111
00:05:28,067 --> 00:05:30,933
Grandpa Xavi,
maybe we should talk to her.

112
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:34,100
Or maybe I should
talk to her myself.

113
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:37,100
Angel, my dear, don't.

114
00:05:37,233 --> 00:05:40,300
You might get caught up in
her resentment toward us.

115
00:05:40,433 --> 00:05:42,167
Let it go.

116
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,500
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

117
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:46,167
I'll find the right time.

118
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:49,400
I'll be the one to talk to her.

119
00:05:49,533 --> 00:05:51,067
I just need the
right opportunity.

120
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:55,200
She may have become rich, Dad,
but her attitude got worse.

121
00:05:55,333 --> 00:05:58,867
I'm sure she still blames us
for her child's death.

122
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,067
Even though the truth is
she can't admit to herself

123
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:05,100
that she's the reason
her life fell apart.

124
00:06:06,667 --> 00:06:12,900
Bev, like I said,
I'll talk to her myself.

125
00:06:13,067 --> 00:06:16,500
Remember,
she's still your sister.

126
00:06:16,633 --> 00:06:17,600
She's my daughter.

127
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:22,600
Maybe I can find a way
to soften her heart.

128
00:06:23,767 --> 00:06:25,733
But for now, while...

129
00:06:25,867 --> 00:06:28,900
her anger is still that intense,

130
00:06:29,033 --> 00:06:31,300
it's probably best
if we're careful.

131
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:41,900
[SOFT TENSE MUSIC]

132
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:53,133
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC]

133
00:07:02,867 --> 00:07:05,733
<i>I hope you can hear the song
I wrote for you, my child.</i>

134
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,967
<i>There isn't a day that
I don't pray to God</i>

135
00:07:15,133 --> 00:07:16,400
<i> wishing you were still alive.</i>

136
00:07:18,933 --> 00:07:22,200
<i>And hoping that one day
we'll meet again.</i>

137
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:30,567
[CELLPHONE RINGS]

138
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,500
<i>- Mr. Montaverde-san.
- Yes.</i>

139
00:07:34,767 --> 00:07:36,233
I can provide those photos.

140
00:07:37,967 --> 00:07:42,100
Just do everything you can
to find my princess, please.

141
00:07:42,233 --> 00:07:45,200
- Thank you very much.
- Yeah.

142
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,267
Thank you.

143
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,500
[SNIFFLES]

144
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:53,167
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:08:05,867 --> 00:08:10,433
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

146
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,400
This is exciting.

147
00:08:21,733 --> 00:08:23,000
We have so many visitors.

148
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:24,733
- Wow!
- Hello!

149
00:08:24,867 --> 00:08:26,267
Hello!

150
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,700
You know, I'm so happy.

151
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:30,633
This was your
grandmother's dream too.

152
00:08:31,367 --> 00:08:32,500
- And it finally came true.
- Yes.

153
00:08:32,633 --> 00:08:33,800
And the bucket list too.

154
00:08:33,933 --> 00:08:34,967
- Yes.
- That's right.

155
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:37,033
- We can check it off now.
- We've checked it off.

156
00:08:37,167 --> 00:08:38,400
There are our guests.

157
00:08:38,533 --> 00:08:39,533
They're waiting for us.

158
00:08:39,667 --> 00:08:41,233
We've completed our
bucket list too.

159
00:08:41,367 --> 00:08:41,867
Here we go.

160
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,667
We're about to begin.

161
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,033
<i> ♪ Repeat all night ♪</i>

162
00:08:45,167 --> 00:08:46,700
Yes.

163
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:48,733
<i> ♪ I know that I'll... ♪</i>

164
00:08:48,867 --> 00:08:50,200
Yes!

165
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:54,700
Welcome to Gran Vista Resort,
everybody.

166
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:55,700
[APPLAUSE CONTINUES]

167
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,467
Thank you.

168
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,967
Congratulations to all of you!

169
00:08:59,100 --> 00:08:59,967
Oh, thank you. Thank you.

170
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,400
Our grand opening here

171
00:09:01,533 --> 00:09:02,700
at Gran Vista finally
pushed through.

172
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:05,133
That's right.
You know, thank you all so much.

173
00:09:05,267 --> 00:09:07,800
Even though we can't pay much,
you're still here with us.

174
00:09:07,933 --> 00:09:11,900
Oh, my. And to all our guests,
we'll all share a meal later.

175
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:13,933
I'll be cooking for everyone.

176
00:09:14,067 --> 00:09:15,133
- Wow.
- Yes.

177
00:09:15,267 --> 00:09:16,467
[ALL APPLAUDING]

178
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,933
All right,
go prepare our welcome drinks

179
00:09:19,067 --> 00:09:20,400
and the food too.

180
00:09:20,533 --> 00:09:22,000
Oh, Grandpa Xavi,
congratulations.

181
00:09:22,133 --> 00:09:23,600
- Oh, my.
- Amazing!

182
00:09:23,733 --> 00:09:24,633
Thank you, Zion.

183
00:09:24,767 --> 00:09:26,300
- Thank you for coming.
- Of course.

184
00:09:26,433 --> 00:09:28,567
Hey, how are you? Thank you,
I'm glad you made it.

185
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:31,467
Oh, are you going swimming?

186
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,533
Thank you, Zion.

187
00:09:33,667 --> 00:09:39,267
["FIRST LOVE" BY HEATH,
CLIFFORD, AND MARCO]

188
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:46,933
<i>♪ Do you still remember the days
when ♪</i>

189
00:09:47,067 --> 00:09:52,700
<i>♪ It was just the two of us
together ♪</i>

190
00:09:52,833 --> 00:09:54,067
But the food today
is really delicious.

191
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:57,933
[ANGEL AND ZION LAUGHING]

192
00:09:58,067 --> 00:09:59,067
Look at that.

193
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,033
Do you really think
we'd post that?

194
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,433
[LAUGHING CONTINUES]

195
00:10:02,567 --> 00:10:04,367
- Oh, come on.
- Rose, rose, rose.

196
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,333
- There was even a heart on it.
- There was a heart too.

197
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:07,200
- Heart.
- Heart.

198
00:10:07,333 --> 00:10:09,133
[BOTH LAUGH]

199
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,867
Look at us there.

200
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,133
We look a little awkward there.

201
00:10:14,267 --> 00:10:16,433
[ZION LAUGHS]

202
00:10:18,067 --> 00:10:18,967
There.

203
00:10:20,967 --> 00:10:24,300
It's been so long since I last
saw Captain Serenade.

204
00:10:24,433 --> 00:10:25,733
It's a shame.
I was going to invite him

205
00:10:25,867 --> 00:10:28,000
to Gran Vista's grand opening.

206
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:32,700
Captain Serenade?

207
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:34,133
Your mascot friend?

208
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,367
The one who's a great singer.

209
00:10:40,633 --> 00:10:42,700
Maybe he just moved
to a different spot.

210
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:45,200
Isn't that how it
usually is for buskers?

211
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,300
Oh, right.We need to meet
Mr. Moon tomorrow.

212
00:10:52,433 --> 00:10:54,433
He's picking up the
tickets for Siklab.

213
00:10:54,567 --> 00:10:55,567
Sounds good.

214
00:10:55,700 --> 00:11:00,033
I'd like to meet him
and thank him too.

215
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,733
You'll get your chance tomorrow.

216
00:11:01,867 --> 00:11:02,900
[ZION CHUCKLES]

217
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:15,233
Angel posted a TokiToki video
about Gran Vista

218
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:17,600
that she and her family built
together.

219
00:11:17,733 --> 00:11:21,500
A lot of people related to it,
so visitors came pouring in.

220
00:11:21,633 --> 00:11:24,033
That Angel really is smart
and capable.

221
00:11:24,167 --> 00:11:27,200
I won't be outdone by that girl,
Tyrone.

222
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:29,700
And I don't care
if she's a genius.

223
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:31,100
She's still just a kid.

224
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,600
[INTENSE MUSIC]

225
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:55,300
You know,
Mr. Moon is really weird.

226
00:11:55,433 --> 00:11:57,300
Apparently,
he's suddenly not showing up.

227
00:11:57,433 --> 00:11:59,300
He isn't picking up
the ticket either.

228
00:11:59,433 --> 00:12:01,633
And he doesn't
even want a refund.

229
00:12:01,767 --> 00:12:03,167
He must be some rich nepo baby.

230
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:08,767
<i>If Mr. Moon isn't coming
after all,</i>

231
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:11,133
<i>then you don't need to come here
anymore, Zion.</i>

232
00:12:11,267 --> 00:12:12,833
I'll just quickly buy a cake

233
00:12:12,967 --> 00:12:14,600
because we have a guest
at Gran Vista

234
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:16,233
who's celebrating
their 60th birthday,

235
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:17,433
courtesy of the resort.

236
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:26,467
<i>That's why your resort
is doing so well, Angel.</i>

237
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,333
<i> You treat your guests so well.</i>

238
00:12:29,367 --> 00:12:30,800
<i> All right, Angel.</i>

239
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:32,900
<i> Be careful on your way home.</i>

240
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:34,933
Bye.

241
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,167
Okay. You too.

242
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,433
So, it's you.

243
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:49,067
Angel of Gran Vista Resort.

244
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:55,900
I'm Serina of the
Montaverde Group of Hotels.

245
00:12:57,233 --> 00:12:58,933
Yes, I know who you are.

246
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,433
Really?

247
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:06,467
I wonder what wonderful things
my sister told you about me.

248
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,900
But I'm more interested in you.

249
00:13:11,033 --> 00:13:12,600
I hear you're exceptionally
talented.

250
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:16,833
A 16-year-old
who can run a resort.

251
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:22,733
Auntie, I was just
about to order a cake.

252
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:24,633
Don't call me "Auntie."

253
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,367
I'm not your aunt.

254
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:29,700
We're not related.

255
00:13:32,833 --> 00:13:34,100
I'll just go.

256
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,467
Don't turn your back on me.

257
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,267
I'm still talking to you.

258
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:42,800
- What is it that you want?
- I want you and your family

259
00:13:42,933 --> 00:13:44,433
out of Solmera City.

260
00:13:44,567 --> 00:13:46,433
I want your resort to go under

261
00:13:46,567 --> 00:13:49,433
so I can buy it
for the Montaverde Empire.

262
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:52,900
Our resort is only popular
because of the sunset.

263
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:54,900
Our resort is tiny
compared to yours,

264
00:13:55,067 --> 00:13:58,433
so I hope you'll fight fair.

265
00:13:58,567 --> 00:14:02,533
And what exactly do you mean
by that?

266
00:14:02,667 --> 00:14:04,933
Mama Bebe, Grandpa Xavi,
and I already know

267
00:14:05,067 --> 00:14:06,733
that you were the one
who sent those boys

268
00:14:06,867 --> 00:14:08,833
to sabotage our resort.

269
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:10,833
[INTENSE MUSIC]

270
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:15,033
Be careful what you say

271
00:14:15,167 --> 00:14:17,533
especially when you have
no proof.

272
00:14:17,667 --> 00:14:19,833
We're not going to sue you.

273
00:14:19,967 --> 00:14:22,367
I just want you to know
that we know.

274
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:25,267
That's why you used kids
to do it, right?

275
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:26,833
So you'd avoid getting sued.

276
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:29,333
How dare you?

277
00:14:32,567 --> 00:14:34,133
Look what you did, you little...

278
00:14:34,267 --> 00:14:38,033
[INTENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

279
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:42,767
[HOPEFUL MUSIC]

280
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:43,867
Young lady.

281
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,133
Are you okay?

282
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:58,367
Serina, what's going on here?

283
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:01,533
Why are you picking a fight
with a kid?

284
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:04,767
Maybe if you knew who she was,
you wouldn't be defending her.

285
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:06,567
That's the adopted daughter
of my sister and Dad,

286
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,433
the one beating our resort.

287
00:15:08,567 --> 00:15:11,800
[TENSE MUSIC]

288
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:14,567
I was only trying to leave.

289
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,333
Ma'am is the one who stopped me.

290
00:15:16,467 --> 00:15:20,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

291
00:15:20,167 --> 00:15:21,233
It's okay, young lady.

292
00:15:21,367 --> 00:15:22,333
You're free to go.

293
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:40,333
Mom and Grandpa didn't raise me
to pick fights.

294
00:15:40,467 --> 00:15:43,433
Even at school,
even when I'm being bullied,

295
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:44,933
I fight fair, Ma'am.

296
00:16:19,867 --> 00:16:20,867
Keep reading all you want.

297
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,033
You're still idiots.

298
00:16:23,133 --> 00:16:23,733
Give me that.

299
00:16:23,867 --> 00:16:24,700
What's this?

300
00:16:25,767 --> 00:16:27,133
Go home, idiots.

301
00:16:30,567 --> 00:16:32,667
Is what you said really true?

302
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:36,733
That Calix bought Angel
and Zion's concert tickets?

303
00:16:36,867 --> 00:16:39,000
Yes, for 15,000 pesos.

304
00:16:39,133 --> 00:16:40,367
That's what Raviel said.

305
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,533
He told me earlier in class.

306
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:45,633
Anyway, I need to know
the truth.

307
00:16:49,067 --> 00:16:50,433
So, Dash...

308
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:55,933
Did you really kiss Janine?

309
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:56,867
Who?

310
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,100
That loser student
from Section Acacia

311
00:17:00,233 --> 00:17:03,167
people say she only showers
every other day.

312
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,133
[BOTH LAUGH]

313
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:07,933
- What? She looks dirty.
- Yuck, Bro! No way!

314
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:11,100
What?

315
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:12,300
See?

316
00:17:12,433 --> 00:17:13,133
No way.

317
00:17:13,267 --> 00:17:14,467
It says that's a lie.

318
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:15,367
Gross.

319
00:17:15,533 --> 00:17:17,733
Because you're not
telling the truth.

320
00:17:17,867 --> 00:17:18,800
Well? Answer it.

321
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,233
What?

322
00:17:23,367 --> 00:17:24,767
Come on, Dash.

323
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,667
It's such a basic question,
and you still can't answer it.

324
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,800
That's why you're
stuck in row four.

325
00:17:29,933 --> 00:17:31,100
Fine, Calix.

326
00:17:31,233 --> 00:17:32,100
Yes.

327
00:17:32,233 --> 00:17:33,733
But it was just a peck, okay?

328
00:17:33,867 --> 00:17:35,367
A kiss.

329
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,400
[LAUGHTER]

330
00:17:37,533 --> 00:17:40,167
Janine and Dash.
Janine and Dash.

331
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:43,133
So you're into girls
who don't shower.

332
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:45,900
What about you, Calix?

333
00:17:49,267 --> 00:17:51,200
I mean, we've all played
already.

334
00:17:52,633 --> 00:17:53,600
Your turn now.

335
00:17:54,867 --> 00:17:55,600
And why would I?

336
00:17:56,933 --> 00:17:58,000
And why not?

337
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,200
It's just a game.

338
00:18:01,333 --> 00:18:02,967
Unless you're intimidated

339
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:05,133
by this little lie-detector
gadget.

340
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:08,967
That's nothing but a toy.

341
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:12,100
Hey. What's the question?

342
00:18:12,233 --> 00:18:13,000
Bring it on.

343
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,767
So, Calix...

344
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:23,800
Do you have feelings for Angel?

345
00:18:35,933 --> 00:18:36,700
Serina!

346
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:39,033
Serina, wait!

347
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:40,100
What?

348
00:18:40,233 --> 00:18:42,867
Why are you picking a fight
with that kid?

349
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,700
Why are you taking her side?

350
00:18:44,833 --> 00:18:46,233
You don't even know
what happened.

351
00:18:46,367 --> 00:18:48,333
I spoke to the staff inside.

352
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:51,500
They said the girl was sitting
at another table

353
00:18:51,633 --> 00:18:52,633
and you suddenly
went after Angel.

354
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:54,900
Was it because you found out
she's from Gran Vista?

355
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:56,300
And what about you?

356
00:18:56,433 --> 00:18:58,833
Why are you being so nice
to that random teenage girl?

357
00:18:58,967 --> 00:18:59,967
What is it?

358
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,800
Are you longing
for your daughter?

359
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,433
Like every other kid,

360
00:19:04,567 --> 00:19:08,000
you see your dead daughter
in that Angel girl.

361
00:19:08,133 --> 00:19:10,267
- That's enough.
- No, Enrico!

362
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,633
You, defending her

363
00:19:11,767 --> 00:19:15,033
just shows how little you care
about how I feel.

364
00:19:15,167 --> 00:19:17,900
You know she's the adopted
child of my enemies.

365
00:19:18,033 --> 00:19:19,900
And yet, what?

366
00:19:20,133 --> 00:19:21,600
You're defending her.

367
00:19:21,733 --> 00:19:25,200
And she's also the reason
Gran Vista is beating Montaverde

368
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:26,233
in online popularity.

369
00:19:26,367 --> 00:19:29,200
And now you're making me
look like the bad one?

370
00:19:29,367 --> 00:19:31,267
- You're a useless husband.
- Serina.

371
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:34,333
Don't you think
you're overreacting?

372
00:19:34,467 --> 00:19:36,167
You know, in fact,

373
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,333
I'm thinking we shouldn't buy
their land anymore.

374
00:19:38,467 --> 00:19:39,967
I'll talk to our investors

375
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:41,000
so we can put an end
to all this.

376
00:19:41,133 --> 00:19:41,633
No, no, no.

377
00:19:41,767 --> 00:19:42,767
No, Enrico.

378
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:47,033
You know how much
I hate Angel's family.

379
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:49,767
And I would make her life
even more miserable.

380
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:50,933
I will never stop

381
00:19:51,067 --> 00:19:53,733
until their pathetic little
resort goes bankrupt.

382
00:19:53,867 --> 00:19:55,233
And you can't stop me.

383
00:19:55,367 --> 00:19:57,767
- Serina, where are you going?
- What?

384
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,167
I need space from you.

385
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,667
I'll come home tomorrow.

386
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,900
I'm going to find a hotel.

387
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:04,633
Let's go.

388
00:20:04,767 --> 00:20:06,033
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

389
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,567
[ENGINE REVS]

390
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:21,533
Gino?

391
00:20:23,167 --> 00:20:24,300
You need something?

392
00:20:24,433 --> 00:20:26,733
Sir, this can wait.

393
00:20:26,867 --> 00:20:27,467
No, it's fine.

394
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,700
What is it?

395
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:32,033
[INTRIGUING MUSIC]

396
00:20:32,167 --> 00:20:34,233
I'm not sure
if this is the right time

397
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:36,500
to tell you this, Sir.

398
00:20:36,667 --> 00:20:38,333
But...

399
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:39,633
Sir Enrico...

400
00:20:42,567 --> 00:20:44,033
Sir, you need to see this.

401
00:20:44,667 --> 00:20:49,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

402
00:20:56,433 --> 00:20:57,533
Sir, you need to see this.

403
00:20:57,667 --> 00:21:03,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

404
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:14,633
<i>Are you having an affair
with Tyrone?</i>

405
00:21:14,767 --> 00:21:17,900
<i>Is that really
how little you think of me?</i>

406
00:21:18,033 --> 00:21:20,933
<i>You think I'm having an affair
with my driver?</i>

407
00:21:21,067 --> 00:21:23,533
<i>After everything
that we've been through,</i>

408
00:21:23,667 --> 00:21:24,967
<i>even when you nearly took
your own life</i>

409
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:26,567
<i> after losing everything,</i>

410
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:27,933
<i> I was there by your side.</i>

411
00:21:28,067 --> 00:21:30,133
<i>And despite everything
that I did,</i>

412
00:21:30,267 --> 00:21:34,133
<i>you still have the nerve to
accuse me of having an affair?</i>

413
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,033
Serina...

414
00:21:42,333 --> 00:21:44,233
how could you betray me?

415
00:21:44,367 --> 00:21:49,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

416
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:57,300
<i>Coming up tomorrow on
You're My Favorite Song...</i>

417
00:21:57,433 --> 00:21:59,500
You thought I wouldn't be able
to track you down, didn't you?

418
00:21:59,633 --> 00:22:01,400
[TENSE MUSIC]

419
00:22:01,533 --> 00:22:02,600
Enrico?

420
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,600
Shocks, someone's here.

421
00:22:17,567 --> 00:22:23,033
["FIRST LOVE" INSTRUMENTAL]

422
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:26,433
Ma'am, we've received a report

423
00:22:26,567 --> 00:22:27,500
that the yacht belonging
to Mr. Enrico Montaverde

424
00:22:27,633 --> 00:22:29,033
has exploded.

425
00:22:29,167 --> 00:22:29,733
- What?
- At the moment,

426
00:22:29,867 --> 00:22:30,500
we're still searching for him.

427
00:22:30,633 --> 00:22:31,533
What?

428
00:22:31,667 --> 00:22:33,300
What did you say?

429
00:22:33,433 --> 00:22:35,000
My husband's yacht exploded?

430
00:22:36,367 --> 00:22:38,767
["You're My Favorite Song"
INSTRUMENTAL]
